/-!
# Mutation of the standard stratification under the braiding functors

B. Webster, *Knot invariants and higher representation theory*, arXiv:1309.3796v3,
Proposition 6.20: the braiding functor `𝔅_w : D(T^λ) → D(T^{wλ})` (Definition 6.6, ungraded,
between the corners of the red orders `(1, …, ℓ)` and `w(1, …, ℓ)`) sends the standard
stratification of the source to a mutation of the target's: for every upper set `U` of source
loadings, the thick subcategory generated by the images `𝔅_w(S_s)`, `s ∈ U`, equals the thick
subcategory generated by the target standards `S'_{w s}`, `s ∈ U`, where `w s` is the loading
with the blocks of `s` (each red strand with the black strands to its right) permuted by `w`
(`blockTransport`). This is `thickClosure_braidingFunctor_violLoadingStandard`.

The proof is the descending induction of Webster's proof. A loading projective `P_s` maps onto
`S_s` with kernel filtered by the standards above `s` (Corollary 5.22, right form at the red
order `(1, …, ℓ)`), and `𝔅_w(P_s)` is the cut `e(s) V e_{wλ}`, filtered by target standards at
the bottoms of the eligible indices of the braid column of `s` (Lemma 6.11). Those labels are
the block-permuted loadings `w b` with `b ≥ s`, and only one index has `b = s`.

Route hypotheses: those of Lemma 6.11 (`AllFiniteDeltaInjective` for all labels, and
`RowFigureFiveHypotheses`, the injectivity of Lemma 6.8), as for Theorem 6.15.
-/

noncomputable section

